    <DataNode elementId="AT4G31810-MONOMER" textLabel="AT4G31810-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8RXN4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">A few Arabidopsis enoyl-CoA hydratases have been experimentally studied. However they were peroxisomal located and are involved in fatty acid beta oxidation|CITS: [10521521], [16982622]|. One protein, encoded by AT4G31810, was detected in mitochondria and could be a good candidate involved in branched-chain amino acid degradation|CITS: [11743115]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G31810-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G31810.1" />
